# Evaluation outputs. The e1_*.json scorecards ARE tracked: they are results,
# not build artefacts. Each costs a day of the Groq free-tier budget to produce,
# the hosted model can change under the same name, and a scorecard for a prompt
# version that has since been replaced cannot be regenerated at all -- the
# 15 Oct prompt-v3 baseline is the example. HISTORY.md and the research notes
# cite these files by path, so they have to exist in the repo. Anything else
# dropped in this folder is scratch and stays ignored.
data/eval/*
!data/eval/e1_*.json
!data/eval/e5_*.json
!data/eval/e6_*.json
!data/eval/benchmark_v1_*.json
# 17 Nov 2026: the forecast comparison results are cited by path in docs/research/, so they are tracked too.
!data/eval/forecast_fit_*.json
!data/eval/forecast_baseline_check_*.json
!data/eval/forecast_diagnose_*.json
!data/eval/forecast_models_v2_*.json
!data/eval/model_a_v2_*.json
!data/eval/model_a_v2_predictions_*.csv
# 20 Nov 2026, Experiment A (docs/research/expA-protocol-2026-11-20.md): gold answers, model
# replies, executions and scorecards are tracked, like the E1 scorecards (each run costs days of
# the Groq free tier). Snapshots copy the raw archive (about 15 MB each) and stay local, except
# their manifests, which pin the exact data by SHA-256.
!data/eval/expA/
data/eval/expA/snapshots/**
!data/eval/expA/snapshots/**/
!data/eval/expA/snapshots/**/manifest.json
